s absent from the index and that the tool-grant is driven by the routing `exec: AGENT` entry.","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.25,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["index.json contains only six entries (code-quality, completion-verifier, security, spec-alignment, tests, ticket-quality); Grep for 'docs' and 'code-review' in index.json returns no matches for the overlay.","build_prompt_index skips prompts where `not prompt.is_reviewer` (src/rebar/llm/prompting/prompts.py:265) and is_reviewer == (category == 'review') (src/rebar/llm/prompting/prompt_model.py:99, docs/reuse-surface.md:316).","code-review-docs.md declares `category: code-review-pass` (line 9), not `review`, so is_reviewer is False and the overlay is never emitted into the index — its execution_mode is not represented there at all.","code-review-tests.md (an existing agentic overlay) likewise carries `category: code-review-pass` and is absent from index.json, confirming overlays are structurally excluded."],"finding":"The plan's index-regeneration step and its acceptance criterion rest on a false premise: src/rebar/llm/reviewers/index.json does NOT track the code-review-docs overlay prompt, so regenerating it after the execution_mode change produces no diff and the 'index matches updated front matter' AC is vacuous.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd840912b7214d71b","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 'Regenerate src/rebar/llm/reviewers/index.json from prompt front matter'; AC 'The generated reviewer index matches the updated prompt front matter.'","norm_id":"ne514ac492e591ac6","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Author flips execution_mode to agentic, runs regenerate-index expecting a matching diff, and finds index.json unchanged — leaving the AC unverifiable/green for the wrong reason.","Reviewer treats the index AC as proof the runtime tool-grant flipped, when the actual mechanism is the criteria_routing.json `exec: AGENT` entry, not the index."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Replace the index step/AC with: verify (a) the routing `docs` entry now reads `exec: AGENT` and (b) index.json is unaffected because the overlay has category code-review-pass (is_reviewer False); rely on criteria_routing.json — not index.json — as the mechanism that grants repository tools.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile the index.json step/AC with the fact that code-review-docs is an overlay (not is_reviewer) absent from index.json: either drop the index regeneration/AC for this overlay or restate it as a no-drift safety check, and locate the load-bearing execution-mode change in criteria_routing.json's exec field.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.3,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["prompts.py build_prompt_index: 'if not prompt.is_reviewer: continue  # only reviewers populate the selection catalog'","index.json has 6 entries, all is_reviewer:true; search for 'code-review-docs' and 'single_turn' in index.json returns (no matches)","code-review-docs.md front matter: 'category: code-review-pass' with no is_reviewer flag","docs/review-kernel.md:85 — overlays with category:code-review-pass 'stay OUT of the single-pass' reviewer catalog"],"finding":"The plan's index-regeneration step and its acceptance criterion target index.json, but the code-review-docs overlay is not represented there: build_prompt_index (src/rebar/llm/prompting/prompts.py) only emits entries for prompts with is_reviewer:true, and code-review-docs.md is category:code-review-pass (an overlay, not is_reviewer). index.json contains only the 6 is_reviewer prompts (code-quality, completion, security-reviewer, spec-alignment, test-coverage, ticket-quality) — no code-review-docs / no single_turn entries. Regenerating will therefore produce no docs-related change, so the AC 'generated reviewer index matches the updated prompt front matter' is a no-op / unverifiable for this overlay's execution_mode edit.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f32a52307d8aafb7e","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 'Regenerate src/rebar/llm/reviewers/index.json from prompt front matter'; AC 'The generated reviewer index matches the updated prompt front matter.'","norm_id":"n414c29f51689f8dd","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Author runs regenerate-index expecting a docs execution_mode change in index.json and sees no diff, or the prompt-index drift gate passes without reflecting the overlay change — leaving the AC formally unmet."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Note that the overlay's tool-provisioning is driven by criteria_routing.json's `exec: AGENT` (read by code_review/registry), not index.json; keep the regenerate-index run only as a no-drift guard and reword the AC so it does not assert a docs-specific index entry that cannot exist.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"Add a rubric-revision step that explicitly places protected evidence, quotations, historical ticket events, and ADR decision substance outside the documentation criterion's scope, so the exclusion AC maps to a described deliverable.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.075,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["The doc-role step (6) requires abstention only 'when audience, role, or ownership is ambiguous' and does not name protected evidence, quotations, historical ticket events, or ADR decision substance as out-of-scope.","Steps 8 and 9 mention 'protected-evidence' and 'exclusions' as test/eval coverage, but a passing eval case does not by itself add the exclusion to the rubric prose the specialist reads."],"finding":"AC 'Protected evidence, quotations, historical ticket events, or ADR decision substance remain outside the criterion' has no covering step in the Plan body that adds this exclusion to the rubric text; the exclusion only surfaces in the test/eval coverage steps (8/9), not in the rubric-revision steps (3-6).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f7973fe5e32a9d929","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan steps 3-6 vs Acceptance Criteria line 'Protected evidence, quotations, historical ticket events, or ADR decision substance remain outside the criterion.'","norm_id":"n178b4d3e87110e16","priority":0.875,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer writes the rubric revision, wires the tests, but never adds an explicit exclusion clause for quotations/ADR-decision-substance to the rubric text, so the criterion could still flag protected material even though the AC claims it is out of scope."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"In the rubric revision steps, add: 'State that quotations, protected evidence, historical ticket events, and ADR decision substance are out of scope and must not be flagged.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enab